@anon.c8777b812d6b35c09a8e6156f259107b.201 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [1213 x i8] }> <{ [1213 x i8] c"The package indexes to use when resolving dependencies.\0A\0AAccepts either a repository compliant with [PEP 503](https://peps.python.org/pep-0503/)\0A(the simple repository API), or a local directory laid out in the same format.\0A\0AIndexes are considered in the order in which they're defined, such that the first-defined\0Aindex has the highest priority. Further, the indexes provided by this setting are given\0Ahigher priority than any indexes specified via [`index_url`](#index-url) or\0A[`extra_index_url`](#extra-index-url). uv will only consider the first index that contains\0Aa given package, unless an alternative [index strategy](#index-strategy) is specified.\0A\0AIf an index is marked as `explicit = true`, it will be used exclusively for those\0Adependencies that select it explicitly via `[tool.uv.sources]`, as in:\0A\0A```toml\0A[[tool.uv.index]]\0Aname = \22pytorch\22\0Aurl = \22https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu121\22\0Aexplicit = true\0A\0A[tool.uv.sources]\0Atorch = { index = \22pytorch\22 }\0A```\0A\0AIf an index is marked as `default = true`, it will be moved to the end of the prioritized list, such that it is\0Agiven the lowest priority when resolving packages. Additionally, marking an index as default will disable the\0APyPI default index." }>, align 1
